// expect: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// A NESTED FN IS MINTED: a `fn` declared inside a body is a closure record
// built where it is declared — its captures, or an empty record with none —
// so the declaring frame performs `Memory + Alloc`, and a fn declaring
// `!Alloc` around it is a false absence proof. Every maker that returns its
// nested stage (`fn lowpass_filter(sr) = { fn stage(x) = …; stage }`) built
// one with a row of `Pure` until the allocation audit's first frontier run
// (Hβ.effects.allocation-audit-at-the-settle-point).
fn adder(k) with !Alloc = {
  fn add(x) = x + k
  add
}

fn main() = adder(40)(2)
